course: dictionary
lesson: 11628
title: Who decides?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a person who has the power to decide. When you meet one, look at the words around it for clues about who is deciding and what they are deciding. «The referee is the arbiter of the game, so her decision ends every argument.» The referee blows the whistle and settles who was right, so an arbiter must be someone who decides.
explain: Arbiter can also mean someone who decides what is good, like in fashion or taste. «Magazines are arbiters of fashion, so many people copy the clothes they show.» The magazines are not settling a fight here. They are deciding what is stylish, so arbiter can mean a person with great power to decide what is good.
explain: Two phrases are useful to know. A «final arbiter» is the person whose decision is the last word. An «arbiter of taste» is a person whose opinion on what is good style people follow. When you read these phrases, try swapping in the words "judge" or "decider" to see if your meaning still makes sense.
fact: Arbiter means a person who decides or settles something.
fact: An arbiter can settle an argument or decide who is right.
fact: An arbiter can also be someone with great power to decide what is good, such as in fashion or taste.
fact: «Final arbiter» means the person whose decision is the last word.
fact: A referee is the arbiter of a game, because the referee decides the rules and the result.
exercise: «The referee is the arbiter of the game, so her decision ends every argument.» What is an arbiter? | A cook who makes the team's lunch | A small bird that sings at dawn | *A person who decides who is right | A player who scores the most goals
exercise: «Magazines are arbiters of fashion.» What does this mean? | *They have great power to decide what is stylish | They sell old newspapers | They only report on the weather | They are the people who make clothes
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to arbiter? | Sleeper | Gardener | *Judge | Painter
test: «The final arbiter in our argument was Mum, and everyone accepted her decision.» What is a final arbiter? | A cook who stops the argument | *The person whose decision is the last word | A friend who always agrees | A player who has the most points
test: Which phrase means a person whose opinion on good style people follow? | Author of the book | *Arbiter of taste | Painter of the wall | Taster of tea
exam: Which sentence uses arbiter correctly? | *The judge was the arbiter who settled the argument about the goal | We walked to the arbiter to buy some bread | The arbiter ate his lunch very quickly | The arbiter of the cake was very tasty
